  "SOPX": "Ever since childhood I have been passionate about building things. I completed a BSc in Civil Engineering and worked for two years on road projects, where I supervised a drainage design that served about 3,000 residents. I want to study structural engineering because many bridges in my region need assessment and repair, and I want to learn modern monitoring methods.\n\nDuring my final year project I tested concrete beams and compared my results with a simple model. This showed me how important data is for safe design.\n\nAfter my Masters I plan to return home and help assess ageing bridges."
